@startuml
title Research Desk team: dispositions, the bounded revise cycle, and the human gate
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Question" as question #DCEEFF
question : input node
question : token value: the run prompt (String)

state "Draft" as draft #C9E4F7
draft : activity: Researcher agent (structured-v1)
draft : first pass drafts from retrieved context on chain;
draft : revise passes redraft against the Critic's feedback

state "Critique" as critique #C9E4F7
critique : activity: Critic agent (structured-v1)
critique : verdict line mapped to an integer score on chain;
critique : the sentinel short-circuits to score 5, no model call

state "Decide" as decide #FFF0C2
decide : gateway: firstMatch route group
decide : transitions tried in priority order

state "Escalation gate" as gate #FFE0B8
gate : approval: policy owner, quorum 1, no timeout
gate : the run suspends here (runSuspended, exactly once);
gate : encrypted continuation checkpointed to F1r3drive

state "Archive" as archive #C9E4F7
archive : activity: Archivist agent (structured-v1)
archive : files human-authored answers into embers-demo-docs;
archive : the sentinel and unrecognized shapes pass through unarchived

state "Answer" as answer #C8E8D0
answer : output node: the run completes and the
answer : caller receives the final token value

state "Refused" as refused #F6BFC0
refused : final node: the run ends in refusal

[*] --> question : run accepted\n/ token minted at the initial node
question --> draft : completed
draft --> critique : completed
critique --> decide : completed
decide --> answer : #0 accept: completed\n[<latex>output.score \geq 80</latex>]
decide --> draft : #1 revise: completed\n[<latex>\kappa < 3</latex>] / <latex>\kappa{+}{+}</latex>
decide --> gate : iterationLimit\n(disposition rewritten at Decide\nwhen the revise bound is exhausted)
gate --> archive : completed: approved at quorum 1\n/ null payload preserves the token value;\na non-null payload replaces it
archive --> answer : completed\n/ adds archived: true iff a\nhuman answer was filed
gate --> refused : rejected
answer --> [*]
refused --> [*]

note bottom of decide #EAF7EE
A disposition is a token-local label matched against
transition triggers before guards. firstMatch tries
#0 accept first; the kernel evaluates its compare guard
over the JSON observation. #1 revise is unconditional in
the definition — the bracket shows loop.maxIterations = 3,
whose counter <latex>\kappa</latex> lives in the token's execution context.
Up to 3 revise traversals occur; exhaustion is not a
traversal but a rewrite of the disposition to
iterationLimit at the source node.
end note

note right of gate #FFF6C9
No timeout is declared, so no timedOut route exists:
the gate waits indefinitely for a signed approve or
reject command carrying a globally unique decision id.
end note

note left of archive #EAF7EE
Only the gate's completed route reaches Archive: the
#0 accept edge routes Decide straight to Answer, so
accepted model output can never re-enter the retrieval
corpus. Combined with the sentinel pass-through, the
Archivist files exactly the human-authored answers.
The archive node declares the team's only retry policy
(3 attempts, backoff 10 s then 30 s) because ChromaDB
is real infrastructure.
end note
@enduml
